\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 ##\cf4 \strokec4  Phase 4: EV Dashboard & Analysis
\f1\b0 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 ###\cf4 \strokec4  Core EV Calculation
\f1\b0 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \strokec2 ```\cf5 \strokec5 \
EV per unit bet = (win_rate \'d7 2) - 1\
\
Examples:\
- 33% win rate: (0.33 \'d7 2) - 1 = -0.34 (lose $0.34 per $1 bet)\
- 43% win rate: (0.43 \'d7 2) - 1 = -0.14 (lose $0.14 per $1 bet)  \
- 50% win rate: (0.50 \'d7 2) - 1 =  0.00 (breakeven)\
- 53% win rate: (0.53 \'d7 2) - 1 = +0.06 (profit $0.06 per $1 bet)\
\cf2 \strokec2 ```\cf5 \strokec5 \
\

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 ###\cf4 \strokec4  Hourly Rate Calculation
\f1\b0 \cf5 \strokec5 \
Even if marginally +EV, time cost matters:\
\cf2 \strokec2 ```\cf5 \strokec5 \
hourly_ev = (ev_per_bet \'d7 bet_size \'d7 games_per_hour)\
\
Example at 53% win rate, $10 bet, 6 games/hour (10 min/game):\
hourly_ev = 0.06 \'d7 10 \'d7 6 = $3.60/hour\
\
Example at 43% win rate, $10 bet, 6 games/hour:\
hourly_ev = -0.14 \'d7 10 \'d7 6 = -$8.40/hour\
\cf2 \strokec2 ```\cf5 \strokec5 \
\

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 ###\cf4 \strokec4  Variance & Risk of Ruin Analysis
\f1\b0 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \strokec2 -\cf5 \strokec5  Klondike is a binary outcome (win/lose) \'97 model as Bernoulli trials\
\cf2 \strokec2 -\cf5 \strokec5  Calculate bankroll requirements for a given risk of ruin\
\cf2 \strokec2 -\cf5 \strokec5  Standard deviation per game = sqrt(p \'d7 (1-p))\
\cf2 \strokec2 -\cf5 \strokec5  For 53% edge: SD per game \uc0\u8776  0.499, very high variance relative to tiny edge\
\cf2 \strokec2 -\cf5 \strokec5  Kelly criterion for optimal bet sizing: f* = (bp - q) / b where b=1 (net odds), p=win rate, q=1-p\
\

