\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 ##\cf4 \strokec4  Bottom Line
\f1\b0 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\
The critical unknown is the \cf2 \strokec2 **\cf5 \strokec5 draw-1 imperfect-info MCTS win rate\cf2 \strokec2 **\cf5 \strokec5 . If Lonelybot achieves >50% on draw-1 unlimited passes without perfect information, then the game is theoretically beatable by a superhuman AI \'97 but the practical question becomes whether a human (or human-assisted tool) can replicate that performance in a live 1xbet session without violating ToS. If the MCTS rate is <50%, the game is definitively -EV for everyone and the casino profits purely from the information asymmetry inherent in face-down cards.\
\
\cf2 \strokec2 **\cf5 \strokec5 Priority order:\cf2 \strokec2 **\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \strokec2 1.\cf5 \strokec5  Get Lonelybot running on draw-1 unlimited passes\
\cf2 \strokec2 2.\cf5 \strokec5  Run Thoughtful mode (100K+ games) \uc0\u8594  upper bound\
\cf2 \strokec2 3.\cf5 \strokec5  Run MCTS mode (10K+ games) \uc0\u8594  realistic AI ceiling\
\cf2 \strokec2 4.\cf5 \strokec5  Build heuristic player \uc0\u8594  estimate strong human performance\
\cf2 \strokec2 5.\cf5 \strokec5  Calculate EV, hourly rate, bankroll requirements\
\cf2 \strokec2 6.\cf5 \strokec5  Decide if worth pursuing further
